    content: 'When Sofia walked into our classroom on Monday, everyone stared at her. She had long dark hair and wore a colorful dress that was different from what most kids wore. Mrs. Rodriguez introduced her and said Sofia had moved from Mexico with her family.\n\nAt first, Sofia was very quiet. She spoke some English, but she was shy about making mistakes. During group work, she sat alone and looked at her notebook. I noticed she was drawing beautiful pictures of flowers and birds.\n\n"Those are amazing!" I said, pointing at her drawings. Sofia looked surprised but then smiled. "Thank you. My grandmother taught me," she whispered. We started talking, and I learned that Sofia loved art, soccer, and spicy food.\n\nOver the next few weeks, Sofia became more comfortable. She taught us Spanish words, and we helped her with English. She shared her mom\'s homemade tamales with the class, and everyone loved them. I realized that people from different places bring wonderful new things into our lives.',
