    topic: 'Environment',
    content: 'Our school was throwing away too much trash. Every day, the garbage bins were overflowing with plastic bottles, paper, and food wrappers. My friend Leo and I decided to do something about it.\n\nWe asked our teacher, Mr. Park, if we could start a recycling program. He thought it was a great idea and helped us make a plan. First, we placed colorful recycling bins around the school: blue for paper, yellow for plastic, and green for food waste.\n\nThen we made posters to teach students how to sort their trash correctly. We gave a presentation in the school assembly about why recycling matters. "Every bottle you recycle saves energy and helps the planet," I explained.\n\nIt was not easy at the beginning. Some students forgot to use the bins or put items in the wrong ones. But Leo and I kept reminding them. After a month, the amount of trash going to the landfill dropped by forty percent!\n\nOur principal was so impressed that she gave us an award. More importantly, other students started their own environmental projects. Leo and I proved that even kids can make a real difference.',
    content_zh: '我們學校丟了太多垃圾。每天，垃圾桶裡塞滿了塑膠瓶、紙張和食品包裝紙。我的朋友里歐和我決定為此做些什麼。\n\n我們問老師朴老師，能不能開始一個回收計畫。他覺得這是一個好主意，幫我們制定了計畫。首先，我們在學校各處放了彩色的回收桶：藍色放紙張，黃色放塑膠，綠色放廚餘。\n\n然後我們做了海報教學生怎麼正確地分類垃圾。我們在學校集會上做了一個報告，講述為什麼回收很重要。「你回收的每一個瓶子都能節省能源並幫助地球，」我解釋道。\n\n一開始並不容易。有些學生忘了使用回收桶，或把東西放錯桶。但里歐和我不斷提醒他們。一個月後，送往垃圾掩埋場的垃圾量減少了百分之四十！\n\n我們的校長非常印象深刻，頒給了我們一個獎。更重要的是，其他學生也開始了自己的環保計畫。里歐和我證明了即使是孩子也能帶來真正的改變。',
